s($,"bBa","b3g",()=>{var q=A.af("z<Hc>")
return A.b([A.v3(B.V,B.Zy,"Getting started",A.b([A.dp('On the sign-in page, switch to "Start your journey," enter your name, email, and a password, and agree to the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. Depending on how the project is configured, you may be signed in immediately or asked to confirm your email first \u2014 if so, check your inbox for a confirmation link.',"How do I create an account?"),A.dp('The confirmation page will show "Account verified successfully" with a button back to sign in. Sign in with the email and password you chose during setup.',"I confirmed my email \u2014 now what?"),A.dp('Your pathway is your target occupation plus your target country \u2014 e.g. "Registered Nurse \u2192 Canada." Everything else in the app (documents, gaps, tasks, the licensing registry) is organized around this one pathway. You set it up right after signing up, and can change it later from the dashboard.','What is a "pathway"?'),A.dp("Yes \u2014 go to Edit Pathway from the dashboard to update either one at any time.","Can I change my occupation or destination country later?")],q)),A.v3(B.R,B.Zv,"Documents & AI review",A.b([A.dp("PDF, JPG, PNG, and HEIC/HEIF (the format iPhones use for photos). Files must be under 15 MB. Anything else is rejected before it uploads, with a clear message explaining why.","What file types can I upload?"),A.dp("When you upload a document, it's sent to an AI model that reads what's visible on it \u2014 things like a name, a date, or a document type \u2014 and compares that against the requirement you're satisfying. The AI only extracts facts; it never decides whether your document will be accepted anywhere. Every result is clearly marked as provisional. The first time you upload, you'll be asked to explicitly agree to this AI processing \u2014 that's a one-time, separate consent from agreeing to the Terms.","How does AI document review actually work?"),A.dp('It means the document was legible and processed, but the app doesn\'t yet have enough detail about the exact requirement (band scores, credit hours, etc.) to give a real pass/fail. This is deliberate \u2014 the app would rather say "uncertain" than guess and be wrong.','What does "uncertain" mean as a review result?'),A.dp("Check the reason shown on the document card. If it says the scan was too blurry, dark, or cropped, re-upload a clearer photo or scan. If it's a genuine processing error, try again \u2014 if it keeps failing, the AI review feature may not be fully configured yet on this deployment.",'My document was marked "failed" \u2014 what do I do?'),A.dp("Yes \u2014 remove it from the Documents checklist and upload a new one for that same requirement. The old file is deleted from storage, not just hidden.","Can I remove or replace an uploaded document?"),A.dp("That depends on the AI provider's own policy, which is outside this app's control \u2014 see the Privacy Policy's AI-assisted document review section for the current answer.","Is my document data used to train the AI model?")],q)),A.v3(B.bf,B.Zu,"Gaps & tasks",A.b([A.dp("A gap is a specific discrepancy between what you have and what your target occupation/country actually requires \u2014 e.g. an English test score that's one band below what's needed. Each gap is explained in plain language, not left as raw jargon.",'What is a "gap"?'),A.dp('Gaps convert into ordered, trackable tasks \u2014 concrete next actions with an explanation of why each one matters. You work through them from the dashboard\'s "Today" card or the full Tasks list.',"How do tasks get created?"),A.dp("Pending means it's awaiting action or review. Verified means it's been confirmed complete. Rejected means something about it needs to be redone \u2014 check the status note on the task for the specific reason.","What do the task statuses (pending, verified, rejected) mean?")],q)),A.v3(B.R,B.y2,"Registration & licensing",A.b([A.dp("The Registration Tracker follows your own specific pathway step by step. The Licensing Registry is a broader, browsable reference \u2014 every occupation in a category, which body registers it, in every supported country \u2014 useful even before you've settled on a final pathway.","What's the difference between the Registration Tracker and the Licensing Registry?"),A.dp("Teal means verified against a primary source. Amber means directional \u2014 informative, but not independently re-checked, so confirm it with the official body before relying on it. Gray means confirmed not to be a regulated profession in that country.","What do the colored confidence markers mean?"),A.dp("Open a cell in the Licensing Registry that has a checklist icon, work through each step, then submit once everything is checked. You can edit and resubmit later if something changes.","How do I submit a licensing checklist?"),A.dp("No. This app is an organizational and informational tool \u2014 it helps you track documents and understand publicly available requirements. It is never a substitute for the official guidance of the government body handling your application, or for a licensed immigration professional.","Is PathFinder AI a substitute for a licensed immigration lawyer or migration agent?")],q)),A.v3(B.V,B.yb,"Certificates & sharing",A.b([A.dp("It creates a shareable, public link showing a snapshot of your real progress \u2014 which requirements are verified, pending, or rejected. It's a deliberate, one-time snapshot you choose to publish, not a live feed anyone could poll for real-time updates.",'What does "publish a certificate" do?'),A.dp("Yes \u2014 publishing again overwrites the same link with your latest progress, so a link you already shared keeps working and just shows newer data.","Can I update a certificate after publishing it?"),A.dp("Anyone with the link \u2014 it's intentionally public, with no sign-in required, so it's easy to share with an employer or agent. It only ever shows what you explicitly published, never your live account data.","Who can see my published certificate?")],q)),A.v3(B.R,B.y5,"Notifications",A.b([A.dp("Account Settings \u2192 Notifications. Push notifications will also ask your browser or device for permission \u2014 that request only appears after you turn the toggle on, never before.","How do I turn on email or push notifications?"),A.dp("Real inactivity on your pathway \u2014 you won't be messaged just for existing. Reminders only go to accounts that have opted in on that specific channel.","What triggers a reminder?"),A.dp("Turn the relevant toggle off in Account Settings at any time \u2014 it takes effect immediately.","How do I stop notifications?")],q)),A.v3(B.b9,B.ZD,"Account & privacy",A.b([A.dp("Profile menu \u2192 Change profile picture, or Profile \u2192 Picture directly.","How do I change my profile picture?"),A.dp("Edit it on the Profile screen \u2014 you'll get a confirmation link to your new address before the change actually takes effect, so your account can't be locked out by a typo.","How do I change my email address?"),A.dp("Account Settings \u2192 Delete account. You'll need to type DELETE to confirm. This is real and immediate \u2014 your profile, pathway, uploaded documents, and every associated record are permanently removed, not just hidden.","How do I permanently delete my account?"),A.dp("Not voluntarily \u2014 see the Privacy Policy for the full, exact commitment on this and the narrow legal circumstances where disclosure could be required.","Does PathFinder AI share my data with government agencies?"),A.dp("Linked from the sign-in page footer, Account Settings \u2192 Legal, and the About page.","Where can I read the full Terms of Service and Privacy Policy?")],q)),A.v3(B.bf,B.qV,"Troubleshooting",A.b([A.dp("Check the toast/error message that appears \u2014 most commonly it's an unsupported file type or a file over 15 MB. If neither applies and it still fails, try a different browser or a smaller version of the file, and confirm you're signed in.","A document upload isn't working"),A.dp('This shouldn\'t happen \u2014 a real failure is always supposed to resolve to a "failed" status with a reason, never stay stuck indefinitely. If you see this, remove the document and re-upload it.','A document is stuck on "reviewing"'),A.dp("Check spam/junk first. If email notifications are enabled but nothing ever arrives, the email provider may not be fully configured on this deployment yet \u2014 this is a known, honestly-surfaced limitation rather than a silent failure.","I never received a confirmation or reminder email"),A.dp("This happens when the Terms of Service or Privacy Policy has been materially updated since you last agreed to them. Review the changes (linked right there) and accept again to continue \u2014 or sign out if you'd rather not.","The app is asking me to re-accept the Terms/Privacy Policy"),A.dp("Reach out through the contact details on the Privacy Policy or Terms of Service page.","I can't find an answer here")],q))],A.af("z<Hb>"))})
